    {
      "id": "pre-create-sub-objects-for-reinstantiation",
      "name": "PreCreateSubObjectsForReinstantiation",
      "category": "KismetReinstanceUtilities",
      "signature": "PreCreateSubObjectsForReinstantiation(Old To New Class Map, Old Object, New U Object, Created Instance Map, Old To New Instance Map, Ordered List Of Object To Copy)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Old To New Class Map",
          "type": "TMap<UClass*,UClass*>&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Old Object",
          "type": "UObject*"
        },
        {
          "name": "New U Object",
          "type": "UObject*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Created Instance Map",
          "type": "TMap<UObject*,UObject*>&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Old To New Instance Map",
          "type": "TMap<UObject*,UObject*>*",
          "default": "nullptr"
        },
        {
          "name": "Ordered List Of Object To Copy",
          "type": "TArray<TTuple<UObject*,UObject*>>*",
          "default": "nullptr"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "This method will pre-create all non-default sub object needed for a re-instantiation, what is left is to CopyPropertiesForUnrelatedObjects on the created instances map to finish the re-instancing\nIf the re-instancing is done in a big batch and part to the sub object might already be re-instantiated, you will need to provide those via the OldToNewInstanceMap\n@param OldToNewClassMap in case there are subobject that will need new class type\n@param OldObject to pre-create its non-default sub objects\n@param NewUObject where to store those pre-created sub objects\n@param CreatedInstanceMap in/out of the result of all of the pre-created objects\n@param OldToNewInstanceMap optional parameter of the possible re-instanced sub objects if any\n@param OrderedListOfObjectToCopy List of object to copy in order"
    },
    {
